{
	"name": "Resuscitate",
	"type": "maneuver",
	"img": "icons/weapons/daggers/knife-green.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>You may attempt to restore life to a recently deceased target. As an action, you may attempt to resuscitate a creature that has failed a 3rd death save since your last turn. Doing so requires you to be within 5ft of the target and provokes an opportunity attack. You immediately negate the target’s third failed death saving throw, allowing them to try again on their next turn. You may use this ability, again, if the target fails their third death saving throw, again, before the start of your next turn, at the cost of 1 exertion.</p>",
